#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:150
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A PR owner who stalled: tell the owner, then take the stalled PR over."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:144
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A workflow PR, or a PR in a repository with no train, merges directly. A workflow PR needs no approval beyond the batch card (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Workflow PRs, A)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:139
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Add the merge-train label instead of merging; the train lands the batch with one CI run."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:106
#. Diagram label
msgid "All green per rule 1?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:77
#. Diagram label
msgid "Announce the hand-over or the lapse"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:53
#. Diagram label
msgid "Approve the batch card"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:49
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Approves in the merge manager's session only, one card per batch. An approval given in a sibling's session does not authorise a merge."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:228
#. Diagram label
msgid "Code or pins"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:168
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Coordinate, never duplicate. Yes when a thread, agent or open PR already owns this failure: a draft fix PR linked from the main-red issue, an open PR in that repository touching the same files (rule 3), or a sibling's claim in the coordination group. One fixer per cause, never one per repository: a single lower-layer bug can redden every layer above it, so a red that shares a cause with an owned one is owned too."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:191
#. Diagram label
msgid "Dispatch a fixer"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:114
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Do not merge. The next wake reads the checks again."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:96
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Enforce the pacing rule of continual-progress (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Cancel CI): close superseded or duplicate PRs, such as a re-pin whose commits another open PR already carries, and cancel their runs; cancel stale queued runs that never started, never a main push run that has started; ask the owners of P3 PRs to return them to draft."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:107
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every check run on the head SHA has finished, and anything pending blocks; wait for every tier, e2e included. The full tier ran (the No new failures judge, or every full test shard); a draft or fast-tier-only pass never counts. Every judge passes (owner ruling, 2026-11-07): an aggregate job covers only the parts it names, and each test shard's own no-new-failures table lists 0 new failures; with no judge, each check concluded success, skipped or neutral. A cancelled job counts only when a later run of the same workflow on the same head passed that job. merge:watch prints this verdict per PR."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:197
#. Diagram label
msgid "Fix under way"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:54
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "In the merge manager's session only: one card per batch, naming each PR, after its six lines were posted in that chat. An approval given in a sibling's session does not authorise a merge (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Approvals, B)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:227
#. Diagram label
msgid "Infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:186
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Infrastructure is re-run, not fixed: re-run the failed job once. A second failure is real and goes back through the sort; a Pages timeout goes to the site-size work. A train that fails only on infrastructure gets its failed job re-run once. Never cancel a main push run that has started."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:83
#. Diagram label
msgid "Lane released"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:224
#. Diagram label
msgid "Main red"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:143
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge it through merge:guard"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:14
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge manager watch: wake, read the queue live, route"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:19
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge steward"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:138
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge train"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:205
#. Diagram label
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:113
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not green yet"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:210
#. Diagram label
msgid "Nothing"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:164
#. Diagram label
msgid "Nothing to do"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:102
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Offer the card and land only on the owner's tap."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:192
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One fixer agent per cause, never one per repository. Give it the failing run, the cause and the repository: pins out of step go to the next re-pin train on the index; the layer's own bug to a fix PR in that layer; a lower layer's bug to a fix PR in the lower layer, then a re-pin. It opens a draft fix PR, linked from the main-red issue. The fix is a non-content P0 PR and follows the normal merge rules: the six-line request, the owner's batch card, full-tier CI green as judged. Close the loop when the next main run is green and the main-red issue closes. Never silence the failure, and never skip, disable or quarantine a gate or a test."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:174
#. Diagram label
msgid "Owned: coordinate"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:167
#. Diagram label
msgid "Owned?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:48
#. Diagram label
msgid "Owner"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:124
#. Diagram label
msgid "Post the request in chat, then the batch card"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:117
#. Diagram label
msgid "Pre-approved?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:185
#. Diagram label
msgid "Re-run the failed job once"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:65
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read live, never from a stored copy: the open PRs (draft, head, mergeable, owed checks, open owner decisions), the queued and running runs with the age of the oldest, the latest main push run, each PR owner's last push or comment, and every harness repository's open main-red issue with its newest failed runs on main and gh-pages, whether or not the lane holds a PR there (gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/actions/runs?branch=<default>&event=push: the latest completed push run per workflow, conclusion failure). One sweep runs merge:watch over every repository it holds. Liveness duty: acknowledge each new merge request within holding.heartbeatMinutes, and post a heartbeat with each sweep, so siblings can tell a live merge manager from a stalled one."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:64
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read the queue, acknowledge requests"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:208
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ready"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:95
#. Diagram label
msgid "Relieve the runners"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:130
#. Diagram label
msgid "Rides the train?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:207
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturated"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:87
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Saturated: queued runs are 60+ minutes old and nothing has landed, or the owner says the runners are full. Stalled: a PR owner has been silent for 2+ hours. Ready: a merge request is in, with green owed CI. Main red: the main-red issue is open, or the latest completed push run of a workflow on a harness repository's main (or a gh-pages deploy) failed. Otherwise nothing."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:101
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturation meta-merge"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:179
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Sort each failure into one cause before dispatching, because the fix lands in a different place for each. Infrastructure: \"The runner has received a shutdown signal\", a cancelled job, a Pages deploy stuck at syncing_files until it times out. Pins out of step: the failure names a file or test of another layer whose own main already differs. The layer's own bug: it names this layer's own file and fails at this layer's own main. A lower layer's bug: it names a lower layer's file and fails at that layer's main too."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:209
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:149
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled-agent triage"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "Still holding the lane?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:78
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tell every sibling and the owner, and update the durable note: either the session that holds the lane now, or that the lane lapses and each session merges its own green PRs with the owner's approval, still sending the six-line merge request."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:175
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tell the owning thread what the sweep saw (the failing run, and any other repository it reddens), track its PR like any other in the lane, and open no second fixer."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:17
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The loop run by the session that holds the merge-steward lane (actor merge-manager, skill merge-manager-watcher): elected, appointed, or holding it for its own PRs only. Each wake reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and the PR owners live, acknowledges merge requests within the heartbeat, and routes to the train, a direct merge, runner relief, a saturation meta-merge, a stalled-agent takeover, or a fixer for a red main in any harness repository (owner, 2026-11-10: \"That should be a part of merge manager (dispatch an agent to fix them)\", \"Add to process\"). Every merge waits for the owner's own OK, given in the merge manager's session as one card per batch (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Approvals, B). How a sibling finds or elects the merge manager and sends it a request is Process_MergeRequest."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:20
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The merge manager: the one session holding the merge-steward lane, by the owner's word, by election, or for its own PRs only. Each wake it reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and who owns each PR, acknowledges requests within the heartbeat, then routes to the process the queue needs or stays idle. It hands over explicitly when it stops; like any agent it may stall, and the siblings then re-elect."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:198
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The next wake reads main again; the red stays on the sweep until the next main run is green."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:125
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The sibling's six lines go into the merge manager's chat first; a request with no rendered preview and no reason goes back to the sibling (owner ruling, 2026-11-07). Then one card per batch, naming each PR, in priority order: P0 main-red fixes and the re-pin chain, P1 work they unblock, P2 CI speed, P3 the rest."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:60
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The sweep cadence, as a backstop: every 10-15 minutes while a P0 PR is in flight, every 30 minutes otherwise. Otherwise a subscribed PR event, a sibling's merge request, a main run finishing, or a sibling's message wakes it. An agent with no chat to the merge manager (a local agent such as agy) signals on the PR itself: ready for review, the label ready-to-merge, and a signed ready: <head sha> comment; each sweep reads every open PR labelled ready-to-merge in the repositories it watches. Never a polling loop inside a turn."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:59
#. Diagram label
msgid "Timer, PR event, request, main run, or sibling message"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:154
#. Diagram label
msgid "Wake handled"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:86
#. Diagram label
msgid "What does the queue need?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:178
#. Diagram label
msgid "Which cause?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:204
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:131
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes for a folio-assistant PR that does not change .github/workflows/. No for a workflow PR, or a PR in a repository with no train (owner ruling, 2026-11-07, card Train, A)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:118
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when the owner already said to merge this PR when green, so no second card is needed. Otherwise the request goes on the next batch card."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes while the lane is needed (laneNeeded), or while this session manages only its own PRs. No when it stops: the condition no longer holds, or it hands over to a named session."
msgstr ""
